  "difficulty": 3,
  "marks": 1,
  "estimatedSeconds": 90,
  "stem": "The times taken by a kombi to travel from Harare to Chitungwiza are normally distributed with mean 42 minutes and standard deviation 3.5 minutes. In a month the kombi makes 200 such trips. Find the expected number of trips that take more than 47 minutes, giving your answer to the nearest whole number.",
  "answerSpec": {
   "value": 15
  },
  "explanation": "$z = \\frac{47 - 42}{3.5} = 1.429$; $\\mathrm{P}(X > 47) = 1 - \\Phi(1.43) = 0.0764$ (calculator 0.0766). Expected number $= 200 \\times 0.0766 = 15.3$, about 15 trips.",
  "workedSolution": "1. $z = \\frac{47 - 42}{3.5} = 1.429$; $\\mathrm{P}(X > 47) = 1 - \\Phi(1.43) = 0.0764$ (calculator 0.0766). Expected number $= 200 \\times 0.0766 = 15.3$, about 15 trips.",
  "hints": [
   "Find the probability for one trip, then multiply by 200."
  ],
  "modelResponse": {
   "type": "NUMERICAL",
   "value": "15"
  },
  "wrongResponses": [
   {
    "type": "NUMERICAL",
    "value": "185"
   }
  ],
